title: MochiUncle_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite CobblerShop>>

After noticing his own worn-out shoes and remembering his mother's comments about supporting local craftsmen, Raju visits Mochi Uncle's cobbler shop to see if the skilled artisan might need assistance.

The narrow cobbler shop fills with earthy scents of leather and shoe polish. Mochi Uncle sits cross-legged on his low platform, weathered hands moving with practiced precision. Forty years of skilled craftsmanship surround Raju in organized chaos.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: Arre beta, your shoes look like they've walked a thousand kilometers!

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: Come, sit, let me examine what these poor things have been through.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: Every shoe tells a story about its owner's journey.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Mochi uncle, you're right - they are in terrible condition!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But I don't have much money to pay for proper repairs right now.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I was hoping maybe I could learn something just by watching you work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Money? Beta, good shoes are an investment in your future.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Poor footwear leads to back problems, foot pain, and damaged confidence.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: But more importantly - a young person shouldn't walk around in shoes that don't reflect their potential.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's very generous, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But I feel bad taking charity.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Maybe I could help you with something in exchange?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I have some free time and I'd love to learn about your craft.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Help? Child, cobbling isn't child's play.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: These tools are sharp, the work requires years of experience.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: And one mistake can destroy expensive shoes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Customers trust me with footwear that must last for years - it's not a game.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I understand it's serious craftsmanship, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: But surely there are simple tasks I could learn?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'm careful with my hands and I respect the importance of skilled work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: Respect for skilled work? Beta, most young people today think everything should be thrown away.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: And replaced instead of repaired.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: They don't understand that fixing something requires more skill than buying something new.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to learn, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: My father always says that fixing things teaches you to value what you have.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: And understand how things really work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I want to learn that kind of wisdom.

<<HideCharacter>>
As Raju leaves the cobbler shop, the sounds of hammering and stitching still echo in his ears. He carries deep appreciation for the precision required in traditional craftsmanship. Mochi Uncle's skepticism about young people's commitment has only intensified his resolve.

<<set $MochiUncle_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: MochiUncle_Day2
tags: 
position: -75,-229
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite CobblerShop>>

Despite yesterday's introduction to the demanding world of traditional craftsmanship, Raju returns during the morning work period. He hopes to observe how Mochi Uncle organizes his tools and materials.

The cobbler shop radiates methodical preparation in the early morning. Mochi Uncle systematically arranges tools, sorts materials, and inspects yesterday's completed work. The peaceful atmosphere reveals the careful planning that enables traditional craftsmen to maintain consistent excellence.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: Back again, beta?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: I thought yesterday's reality check about the difficulty of traditional craftsmanship might have sent you running.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Smiling">>
MochiUncle: Most young people lose interest when they discover that real skill takes years to develop.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Actually, uncle, watching you work yesterday made me more interested, not less.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I've never seen anyone use simple hand tools to create such precise results.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Beautiful results too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: It's like watching an artist who works with leather instead of paint.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: Artist? Ha! Beta, society doesn't see cobblers as artists.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: We're considered low-status workers who handle dirty shoes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: People need our services but don't respect our skills.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: They want fast, cheap fixes instead of quality craftsmanship.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: How did you learn such detailed techniques?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Did someone teach you, or did you develop these skills through experience?

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: My father was a cobbler, and his father before him.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: I started learning at age eight, sitting right here on this same platform.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: Forty-two years I've been perfecting these techniques.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Sad">>
MochiUncle: But now my own children want nothing to do with the family trade.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: That must be heartbreaking, uncle.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Seeing your life's knowledge and skill not being passed down to the next generation.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: They want office jobs, computer work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Anything that doesn't involve getting their hands dirty.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: They don't understand that traditional crafts create something permanent.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Serious">>
MochiUncle: Something that serves people for years instead of becoming garbage.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's exactly why I want to learn, uncle!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Traditional skills are disappearing, but they contain wisdom.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Wisdom about quality, patience, and taking pride in work well done.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I don't want that knowledge to be lost.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Quizzical">>
MochiUncle: You keep expressing interest in learning, but cobbler training means different levels of skill.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Quizzical">>
MochiUncle: And commitment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "MochiUncle" "Quizzical">>
MochiUncle: What exactly do you think you could contribute to traditional craftsmanship?

<<HideCharacter>>
As their second conversation concludes with Mochi Uncle's direct question, Raju recognizes his persistent interest has moved beyond polite dismissal into serious consideration. The revelation of the craftsman's sadness about his children rejecting the family trade has transformed Raju's motivation from simple curiosity into genuine commitment.

<<set $MochiUncle_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

